@startuml
title Local-First Conflict Handling
start

:Begin local-first reconciliation;
note right
  Operating mode:
  onedrive ~--sync ~--local-first
  or ~--monitor ~--local-first.

  The local filesystem is evaluated first for upload intent.
  ~--local-first changes ordering; it does NOT mean local bytes
  automatically win over an independently changed online file.
end note

:Run DB consistency check against local filesystem first;
:Identify locally modified tracked files;

repeat
  :Take next modified local file;
  :Fetch current online DriveItem metadata before upload;
  note right
    Fresh online state is checked before upload so that processing
    local changes first cannot silently overwrite a genuine remote
    change that happened since the last applied DB baseline.
  end note
  :Evaluate current online state against\nlocal file and last applied DB baseline;
  if (Genuine / unresolved online conflict?) then (yes)
    :Create and verify independent safeBackup copy of local version;
    note right
      LOCAL DATA LOSS PREVENTION

      The local modification is valuable user data. Preserve it before
      resolving a conflict in which the current online canonical item
      cannot safely be overwritten by the original local file.
    end note
    if (Preservation succeeds?) then (yes)
      :Upload safeBackup as a new file;
      note right
        The local modification survives as an independent online file.
        The conflicting canonical online DriveItem is not overwritten.
      end note
      if (~--upload-only?) then (yes)
        :Retain canonical local path;
        note right
          Upload-only mode does not apply the online conflicting version
          back to the local filesystem after preservation.
        end note
      else (no)
        :Apply current online canonical file\nthrough transactional download;
        note right
          Bidirectional result:
          - local modification is preserved as safeBackup
          - current online canonical content becomes canonical locally
        end note
      endif
    else (no)
      :Preservation failed; do not overwrite online canonical;
    endif
  else (no)
    :Upload local modified file normally;
    :Perform post-upload integrity / timestamp reconciliation;
  endif
repeat while (More modified files?) is (yes)

:Scan local filesystem for new items and upload eligible data;
:Reconcile Microsoft OneDrive online state last;
stop
@enduml
